    place("ryogoku", "Ryogoku Kokugikan", "両国国技館", "Tokyo", "JP", ["must-see", "culture"], 35.6971, 139.7935, "Japan's national sumo stadium — the September Grand Tournament (Aki basho) runs ~13–27 Sep, overlapping your second Tokyo stay. Must-see: a ringside afternoon if tickets appear. Tip: not booked on this itinerary; check Japan Sumo Association / NHK for returns the morning of, and sit east-side for the better light."),
    place("shimokitazawa", "Shimokitazawa", "下北沢", "Tokyo", "JP", ["neighborhood", "shopping"], 35.6616, 139.6683, "Tokyo's thrift-and-theater village — record stores, curry shops, vintage floors in every direction. Must-visit: the Bonus Track and Reload complexes. Tip: most vintage shops only open ~12:00; Sundays have the best energy."),
    place("omoide-yokocho", "Omoide Yokocho (Memory Lane)", "思い出横丁", "Tokyo", "JP", ["food", "nightlife", "must-see"], 35.6935, 139.6995, "Post-war yakitori alley glowing under red lanterns beside the Shinjuku tracks. Must-order: charcoal skewers + a draft beer, elbow-to-elbow at a counter. Tip: cash-only at most stalls and a small seat charge is normal; grab stools before 21:00."),
    place("shibuya-sky", "Shibuya Sky", "渋谷スカイ", "Tokyo", "JP", ["must-see", "view"], 35.6585, 139.7024, "Open-air deck 229m above the scramble — glass corners, a rooftop lawn, Fuji at sunset when clear. Must-do: the corner directly over the crossing at golden hour. Tip: tickets go live exactly 4 weeks ahead at midnight JST and sell out in minutes — in early September sunset is ~18:05, so book a 17:00–17:30 entry. No tripods."),
    place("ueno-park", "Ueno Park", "上野公園", "Tokyo", "JP", ["park", "culture"], 35.7147, 139.7733, "Tokyo's museum mile on a wooded hill — Tokyo National Museum, Kaneiji, Shinobazu lotus pond. Must-see: the lotus pond from Bentendo hall if you detour. Tip: spare-time only on this route; Ameyoko is at the park's southern tip, so a 20-min loop is the realistic add-on."),
    place("ghibli", "Ghibli Museum", "三鷹の森ジブリ美術館", "Tokyo", "JP", ["must-see", "culture", "park"], 35.6962, 139.5703, "Miyazaki's whimsical museum in Mitaka — tickets only via advance sale on the 10th of the previous month (10:00 JST, Lawson), no door sales. Not on this itinerary unless returns appear."),
    place("inokashira", "Inokashira Park", "井の頭恩賜公園", "Tokyo", "JP", ["park", "nature"], 35.7000, 139.5750, "Swan-boat lake park whose bridges and benches star in countless anime. Must-do: 30 minutes in a pedal swan. Tip: local legend says boating couples break up — consider yourselves warned."),
    place("hozenji", "Hozenji Yokocho", "法善寺横丁", "Osaka", "JP", ["neighborhood", "culture", "food"], 34.6678, 135.5025, "Mossy lantern alley near Dotonbori."),
    place("shinsaibashi", "Shinsaibashi", "心斎橋", "Osaka", "JP", ["shopping", "neighborhood"], 34.6750, 135.5013, "Major shopping arcade next to Namba."),
    place("amerikamura", "Amerikamura", "アメリカ村", "Osaka", "JP", ["neighborhood", "shopping", "nightlife"], 34.6728, 135.4985, "Youth fashion and easy dinner near Shinsaibashi."),
    place("roppongi", "Roppongi", "六本木", "Tokyo", "JP", ["neighborhood", "nightlife"], 35.6628, 139.7314, "International nightlife-and-art district — Mori Art Museum, izakaya towers, late bars. Tip: eat on the Roppongi Hills / Azabudai side; the club strip is skippable."),
    place("azabudai", "Azabudai Hills", "麻布台ヒルズ", "Tokyo", "JP", ["shopping", "culture", "architecture"], 35.6605, 139.7400, "Heatherwick-designed 'urban village' under Japan's tallest skyscraper (330m Mori JP Tower). Best shot: Tokyo Tower looming over the central garden plaza. Tip: teamLab Borderless is in the basement — timed tickets only."),
    place("tokyo-tower", "Tokyo Tower", "東京タワー", "Tokyo", "JP", ["must-see", "view", "icon"], 35.6586, 139.7454, "The 333m orange lattice icon — prettiest after dark under its warm 'Landmark Light'. Best angles: straight up from the base, the Tofu Ukai stairs, Shiba Park's lawns. Tip: photographing it from outside is free and often beats paying to go up."),
    place("kabukicho", "Kabukicho", "歌舞伎町", "Tokyo", "JP", ["nightlife", "neighborhood"], 35.6950, 139.7026, "Japan's loudest nightlife quarter — pachinko halls, host-club billboards, the Godzilla head. Best shot: the red Kabukicho gate with the neon canyon behind. Tip: ignore street touts completely; pick venues yourself."),
    place("shinjuku-gyoen", "Shinjuku Gyoen", "新宿御苑", "Tokyo", "JP", ["park", "nature", "must-see"], 35.6852, 139.7101, "Former imperial garden splicing French, English and Japanese landscapes into Tokyo's best deep breath. Must-see: the pond-and-pavilion view in the Japanese garden. Tip: ¥500; through September open to 18:00 (last entry 17:30), closed Mondays; no alcohol allowed."),
    place("tocho", "Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building", "東京都庁", "Tokyo", "JP", ["view", "must-see"], 35.6896, 139.6917, "Free observatory at 202m in the twin-towered city hall. Must-see: Shinjuku's neon grid at blue hour — Fuji silhouette on clear days. Tip: the South Deck runs to 22:00; short security check, no booking needed."),
    place("yoyogi", "Yoyogi Park", "代々木公園", "Tokyo", "JP", ["park", "nature"], 35.6711, 139.6949, "Tokyo's big informal lawn — picnics, buskers, and weekend dance crews under the trees. Must-see: the Meiji-jingu-side path as a green shortcut. Tip: cut through the park between the shrine and Takeshita rather than walking the road; Thursday morning will be quiet."),
    place("cross-shinjuku-vision", "Cross Shinjuku Vision (3D Cat)", "クロス新宿ビジョン", "Tokyo", "JP", ["icon", "neighborhood"], 35.6912, 139.7018, "The giant 3D calico cat that naps, stretches and meows from a curved screen over Shinjuku's east exit. Best view: from the Studio Alta crossing corner. Tip: it appears every few minutes between ads — wait one loop."),
    place("shin-okubo", "Shin-Okubo Koreatown", "新大久保", "Tokyo", "JP", ["food", "neighborhood"], 35.7013, 139.7001, "Tokyo's Koreatown — hotteok, cheese-dog stalls, K-pop shops, and Korean cosmetics one JR stop north of Shinjuku. Must-try: a street hotteok if you still have room after Golden Gai. Tip: 10 minutes' walk north of Gracery; optional only — do not force it after a late arrival night."),
    place("shibuya-parco", "Shibuya PARCO", "渋谷PARCO", "Tokyo", "JP", ["shopping", "must-see"], 35.6619, 139.6983, "Culture-led department store. Must-visit: the 6F pop-culture floor — Nintendo TOKYO, Pokémon Center Shibuya, JUMP SHOP and the Capcom Store in one lap. Tip: queues shrink on weekday afternoons; tax-free counter with passport."),
    place("miyashita-park", "Miyashita Park", "宮下パーク", "Tokyo", "JP", ["park", "food", "shopping"], 35.6616, 139.7011, "Rooftop lawn stretched over a mall along the train tracks, minutes from Shibuya Station. Best combo: rooftop coffee, then the retro Shibuya Yokocho eateries at street level. Tip: clean toilets and a breather before your Shibuya Sky slot."),
    place("bonus-track", "Bonus Track / Reload", "ボーナストラック / リロード", "Tokyo", "JP", ["shopping", "neighborhood", "food"], 35.6610, 139.6672, "Twin low-rise complexes built over Shimokitazawa's buried rail line — indie publishers, natural wine, coffee roasters, outdoor tables. Tip: the best rest stop in Shimokita; most shops open from ~11:00–12:00."),
    place("senkyaku-banrai", "Senkyaku Banrai (Toyosu)", "千客万来", "Tokyo", "JP", ["food", "market"], 35.6450, 139.7842, "Edo-styled food hall beside Toyosu's wholesale market. Best pick: a seafood bowl without Tsukiji's queues. Tip: quieter after 13:00 once the tour groups roll out."),
    place("harmonica", "Harmonica Yokocho", "ハモニカ横丁", "Tokyo", "JP", ["food", "neighborhood"], 35.7033, 139.5792, "Post-war alley grid of ~100 micro-bars and counters by Kichijoji station. Must-do: a shoulder-to-shoulder counter lunch. Tip: sleepy at noon, izakaya-loud after 17:00; carry cash."),
    place("nakano-broadway", "Nakano Broadway", "中野ブロードウェイ", "Tokyo", "JP", ["shopping", "culture"], 35.7093, 139.6652, "Four floors of otaku commerce — dozens of Mandarake specialty stores, vintage toys, anime cels, secondhand luxury watches. Must-see: the vintage figure and cel shops upstairs. Tip: most shops only open from ~12:00 — don't come earlier."),
    place("teamlab-borderless", "teamLab Borderless", "チームラボボーダレス", "Tokyo", "JP", ["culture", "must-see"], 35.6606, 139.7403, "Borderless digital art beneath Azabudai Hills — the works wander between rooms and there is no map. Must-see: Bubble Universe. Tip: timed tickets required; allow 90+ minutes and wear shoes for dark mirrored floors."),
    place("tofu-ukai", "Tofu Ukai stairs (Tokyo Tower)", "とうふ屋うかい", "Tokyo", "JP", ["icon", "view"], 35.6573, 139.7448, "The stone steps beside the Ukai tofu restaurant that stack Tokyo Tower directly overhead. Best shot: low angle from the bottom step after dark. Tip: it's a working restaurant entrance — shoot fast, quietly, and step aside for guests."),
    place("shiba-park", "Shiba Park", "芝公園", "Tokyo", "JP", ["park", "view"], 35.6548, 139.7485, "Open lawns with the classic wide 'tower above the trees' composition. Tip: Zojo-ji temple's gate two minutes away pairs the old temple and the lit tower in one frame."),
    place("shinkyo", "Shinkyo Bridge", "神橋", "Tokyo", "JP", ["icon", "must-see"], 36.7536, 139.6004, "Vermilion sacred bridge arcing over the Daiya River at the entrance to Nikko's shrine district. Best shot: from the modern road bridge just downstream — free. Tip: paying to walk on the bridge adds little; the photo is from the side."),
    place("nihonbashi", "Nihonbashi", "日本橋", "Tokyo", "JP", ["neighborhood", "shopping", "icon"], 35.6840, 139.7744, "The 1911 bridge from which every road in Japan is measured — now roofed by an expressway — beside the Coredo Muromachi complex. Must-see: the kilometer-zero plaque, then Pokémon Center DX. Tip: the adjoining Pokémon Café is reservation-only, weeks ahead."),
    place("yurakucho", "Yurakucho Yakitori Alley", "有楽町 焼き鳥横丁", "Tokyo", "JP", ["food", "nightlife", "must-see"], 35.6751, 139.7630, "Smoky yakitori and izakaya arches under the JR viaduct between Ginza and Hibiya. Must-do: skewers + a highball at an outdoor table as trains rumble overhead. Tip: cheaper and rowdier than Ginza next door; some counters add a small seat charge."),
    place("komachi-dori", "Komachi-dori", "小町通り", "Tokyo", "JP", ["shopping", "food"], 35.3192, 139.5510, "Kamakura's snack-and-souvenir lane from the station toward Hachimangu shrine. Must-try: shirasu (whitebait) bites and sweet-potato soft cream. Tip: eat standing by the stall — strolling-and-chewing is frowned on here."),
    place("kamakurakokomae", "Kamakurakokomae crossing", "鎌倉高校前", "Tokyo", "JP", ["icon", "must-see"], 35.3066, 139.5004, "The seaside Enoden crossing immortalized by Slam Dunk's opening credits. Best shot: green train, crossing gate and ocean from the inland corner. Tip: it's a tiny residential junction — stay off the road; trains pass every ~12 minutes."),
